  "worked_solution": "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=-2$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot (-2)+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le -3 & <8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=-2$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=-2$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=2$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot 2+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 5 & <8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=2$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=2$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=5$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\le 2a+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 2\\cdot 5+1 & <8 \\\\ -3\\le 11 & <8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=5$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=5$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.",
